index 1eafeebdd5..5d732b2c5a 100644
--- a/website/docs/user-guide/features/tools.md
+++ b/website/docs/user-guide/features/tools.md
@@ -284,6 +284,29 @@ backends that cannot hand a running command over, the command keeps today's
 behavior and runs in the foreground until it exits or times out. A value at or
 above the command's timeout has no effect.
 
+### Background processes across a gateway restart
+
+A gateway that stops kills its background processes. On a graceful restart
+(`hermes gateway restart`, `SIGUSR1`, or `SIGTERM` with
+`gateway.sigterm_restart_wait`) it can instead hand the processes of chosen
+backends to the next gateway:
+
+```yaml
+terminal:
+  process_handoff_backends: [ssh]   # [] (default) = stop them all
+```
+
+The processes keep running. The next gateway that starts on the same
+`HERMES_HOME` reattaches them: it keeps reading their output from where the
+old one stopped, keeps the same `session_id`, and still delivers the
+`notify_on_complete` notice to the chat that started them. Background
+processes started with `background=true` on a non-local backend are handed off
+by Hermes itself; a plugin backend can hand off its own processes by
+registering a reattach provider. Processes on the local backend run inside the
+gateway's host or container and always stop with it, so run long jobs on a
+listed backend when the gateway may restart. A process that the next gateway
+cannot reattach is reported once as `lost`.
+
